      "takeaway": "UniTracker addresses whole-body motion tracking on humanoids, where MLP policies trained under partial observations show limited expressiveness and orientation drift. Its three-stage framework first learns a privileged teacher policy, then trains a CVAE-based universal policy with a global motion latent aligned to a full-observation encoder, and finally fine-tunes a student via a lightweight adaptation module supporting per-instance and batch adaptation. The abstract reports validation in simulation and on a Unitree G1 humanoid, claiming better tracking accuracy, motion diversity, and deployment robustness than current baselines, without giving numbers. Inspect how the latent alignment is enforced and how adaptation is scoped.",
